# Image TODO: hami-resource-model-gpumem-gpucores-v1.png

## Purpose
Teach the HAMi resource model visually: one physical GPU divided into gpumem (MB of
VRAM) blocks and gpucores (percent of compute) wedges, shared by several tenants.

## Composition breakdown
- Center: one large neon-green GPU card, divided vertically into a memory half and a
  compute half.
- Memory half: five stacked blocks each labeled "gpumem: 4000 MB", filling a 24 GB
  total bar.
- Compute half: a circular gauge split into percentage wedges, one highlighted at
  "gpucores: 30%".
- Three small pod boxes ("tenant A", "tenant B", "tenant C") pointing to different
  memory blocks and compute wedges, showing independent slices of the same card.
- Caption: "one 24 GB L4 → many isolated tenants, each with its own gpumem + gpucores".

## Gemini prompt
Create a flat technical diagram illustrating the HAMi GPU resource model on one
physical GPU. Draw a single large bright-green GPU card divided vertically into a
memory half and a compute half. In the memory half, stack five blocks each labeled
"gpumem: 4000 MB" filling a 24 GB total bar. In the compute half, draw a circular
gauge split into percentage wedges with one wedge highlighted and labeled "gpucores:
30%". Add three small pod boxes labeled "tenant A", "tenant B", and "tenant C", each
pointing with a thin arrow to a different memory block and compute wedge, showing
independent slices of the same card. Add a caption "one 24 GB L4 → many isolated
tenants, each with its own gpumem + gpucores". Style: flat technical illustration,
dark navy background (#0D1117), electric blue (#2F81F7) and neon green (#39D353)
accents, off-white (#E6EDF3) labels, subtle hexagonal grid texture at 10% opacity, no
photorealism, no gradients on solid elements, clean sans-serif labels, developer
education platform aesthetic. Aspect ratio 16:9.
